      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk i get the systemic stuff but it feels like you're kind of brushing off what people actually see. like, if you look at certain neighborhoods or even specific groups, there are just different patterns in how they prioritize school or study habits. even if it's not \"biological,\" can't we at least say that cultural differences in how families approach education are a legitimate part of why the scores differ? it feels like ignoring that is kind of ignoring reality.",
